diff --git a/dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md b/dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md
index 1b11b42..4d5d838 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md
@@ -88,3 +88,10 @@ General host and tool changes first needed here; each applies to every game:
 - The silent first minute of sound.
 - development.md calls SDK 7.3.2 "the oldest so far"; Mario Kart 8 Deluxe (SDK 4.4.0) is older now.
 - `game.tsv` says values marked "Mario's" are not measured yet, but none is marked.
+
+
+## Experimental launcher display profile
+
+The opt-in `DM_ODYSSEY_DISPLAY_PROFILE=launcher` rewrite pairs four original-word-checked observation gates with the host's `ODYSSEY_DISPLAY_V1` controls. It supports stock, 720p, 900p and 1080p targets plus optional vertical FOV extension to 4:3. The host reads the choice after the launcher and preloader join, verifies the exact main build and paired gates, checks the selected private graphics-quality overlay hash, then changes only the saved dimension arguments and projection S2/S3 values. The original projection setter recalculates its caches and frustum. Square and already-4:3 inputs are skipped. The iOS view and touch normalization use the accepted picture aspect.
+
+Stock/off leaves the register frame and existing overlays unchanged. Handheld mode ignores stale display choices. The quality overlays preserve all non-dimension fields; no shader source, compiler options, cache epoch or PSO key schema changes. The full dynamic quality ladder still applies, so a target is not a per-frame resolution guarantee. Native CPU/frame fixtures exist; iPad scene attachments, HUD/cutscene correctness, frame pacing and performance remain unvalidated. Keep the original Guest and RomFS for rollback. Higher modes require separately coordinated memory pools and are not implied by this capability.
